# A table file IS a plugin. Drop one in this folder, drop the underscore, and it
# appears in the Alphabet picker named after the file - no preset to write.
#
# One `code=text` line per glyph, hex on the left. Lines that do not parse are
# ignored, so comments, blank lines and an assembler's own directives all cost
# nothing. A value in [brackets] names a code that spells nothing - it reads in
# the text as its own `[$2A]` like any other non-letter, and the name is what
# captions its button on the insert row.
#
# For the reversed order an assembler writes (`A=20`), name this file from a
# preset with `order = "text-first"` - see `_table.toml`.
00=A
01=B
02=C
03=D
04=E
05=F
06=G
07=H
08=I
09=J
0A=K
0B=L
0C=M
0D=N
0E=O
0F=P
10=Q
11=R
12=S
13=T
14=U
15=V
16=W
17=X
18=Y
19=Z
1A= 
1B=.
1C=,
1D='
1E=!
1F=?
# A tile that draws something but spells nothing.
2A=[star icon]
